  "note": "Triennial election of the 13 electoral divisions of Ballymoney rural district, one member each, polled on 5 June 1952. Seventeen candidates were nominated for thirteen seats, but withdrawals left Dervock as the only contest. Liggett; Peden. Mr. Ernest Lee withdrew in Enagh, Seacon and Kirkmoyle, leaving those divisions uncontested."
